{% extends "base.j2" %}

{% block content %}
    <section class="about">
        <figure class="about-figure">
            <img class="about-photo" src="/static/imgs/me-openai.webp"
                 alt="Portrait of {{ site.author }}" width="180" height="180">
            <figcaption>How ChatGPT imagines me.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div>
            <h1>{{ site.author }}</h1>
            <p>
                I'm a self-taught developer and hacker. My journey into programming
                started when I was 10, after I picked up a copy of
                <cite>Webmaster's Handbook</cite> from 1997.
            </p>
            <p>
                That book introduced me to HTML, and I quickly started making my own
                little websites. A couple of years later, at 12, I moved on to PHP
                because I wanted to make those websites a little less boring and a
                lot cooler.
            </p>
            <p>
                I had no idea where it would lead. I just liked making things.
            </p>
            <p>
                Later, I went to John Bauer College, a school with an early focus on
                IT, entrepreneurship, and practical programs. There I studied web
                design, programming (Java and PHP), networking, from server racks and
                Cisco routers to writing RIP routing tables, digital technology and,
                yes, Linux.
            </p>
            <p>
                After graduating, I switched from Windows to Linux and never looked
                back.
            </p>
            <p>
                Since then, I've kept learning mostly by building things, breaking
                things, and figuring out why they broke. I've worked with everything
                from web development and Python to Linux, networking, servers,
                containers, and low-level systems.
            </p>
            <p>
                These days, I tend to build the things I wish existed, automate the
                things I find annoying, and occasionally go down a rabbit hole just
                because I want to know how something works.
            </p>
            <p>
                I'm currently deep in vibe-code mode, working on a mix of tools,
                websites, Linux projects, and other weird little ideas that probably
                didn't need to exist, but they do now.
            </p>
            <p>Made in Sweden.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

{% endblock %}
